  "bridgeRouteRisk": {
    "tier": "external-validated-network",
    "summary": "ZCHF cross-chain deployments are reviewed through Chainlink CCIP Burn/Mint token pools (BurnMintTokenPool 1.5.1 on all eight networks, allowList disabled). Frankencoin's CCIPAdmin contract manages token-pool configuration through qualified-voter governance proposals and vetoes, but cross-chain transfer execution still depends on Chainlink CCIP as an external validation and messaging network. Per-chain pool addresses were verified on-chain 2026-07-17: the Ethereum TokenAdminRegistry maps ZCHF to pool 0x9359cd75549DaE00Cdd8D22297BC9B13FbBe4B79, and each L2 token registers pool 0x7CBac118B3F299f8BE1C3DBA66368D96B37D7743 as an approved minter (verified on Optimism, Base, and Gnosis). Pinned totalSupply reads on 2026-07-21 sum to 34,131,422.668749966359367170 ZCHF across the eight deployments; the seven CCIP destination mints sum to 3,697,677.829406945936079760 ZCHF, or 10.83364695%, so the Chainlink CCIP common-mode exposure is measured and remains above the 10% materiality threshold.",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-07-21",
    "reviewer": "KIMI ANCHOR-EV Safety Score V9 bridge route review; SOL-KEYSTONE supply attribution (2026-07-21)",
